sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 25-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (referee re-score) — Morphometric validation: 8/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "The v1 sidecar lists 25 measurements, all `derived_from: script`, every `reference_source` ending in '& Lean 4 Theorem N' (the suite's own restatement), and 23 of 25 with `reference_value` identical to `value` because `ref` is computed by the same expression (abs_error 0.0 in the KG payload). The two that differ are not empirical either: Law 3's 4.7002 is a mis-transcription of exp(40/25.85) = 4.6992, and Law 7's 0.3679 is the N -> infinity asymptote of the quantity whose finite-N value the script computes. No measurement is compared with a value measured on an organism, an experiment, an active-matter trial, or a figure in any cited paper; the one set of numbers that originates outside this script (Law 17's S_6 causal-emergence values) is copied from the repository's own earlier run rather than recomputed or sourced to Hoel. The replacement sidecar written with this audit re-derives every value independently and records a reference only where an independent one exists (Laws 2, 3, 7, 8, 17, 18, 20); the other 18 are reported without a reference and annotated as model-internal. Residual credit for the values being arithmetically correct and reproducible." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L989–L1010: verified_measurements[0]: value_num 91.0, ref_num 91.0, abs_error 0.0, within_5pct true. The KG publishes self-referential zero-error comparisons as validated measurements <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L989-L1010>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L380–L384: run_all: assert abs(metric - ref) < 0.01 is the only validation; with ref computed from the same expression it is unfalsifiable for 23 laws <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L380-L384>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml L116–L122: Measurement 17: Delta CP 0.1191 with reference 0.1191 'Hoel (2026) Patterns 7:101472'; the number is from sorting-morphogenesis/PLATONIC_SPACE_CLAIMS_EVALUATION.md L113, the repository's own prior computation, not from Hoel <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml#L116-L122>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml L165–L179: Measurements 24-25: 0 nM Ca2+ error (identity) and l2 error 4 (64/16) with references 0 and 4 from the same arithmetic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml#L165-L179>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml L18–L24: Measurement 3: value 4.6992 vs reference 4.7002 attributed to Pietak & Levin; the reference is a transcription error of the same exp(40/25.85), not a published number <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml#L18-L24>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml L39–L45: Measurement 6: 0.82 + 0.12 = 0.94 bits with reference 0.9400 'Finzi, Kolter & Wilson (2026)'; the constants are invented in the script (L81) and no such numbers are sourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml#L39-L45>",
            "morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml L4–L10: Measurement 1: value 91.0, reference_value 91.0, reference_source 'Levin (2019) ... & Lean 4 Theorem 1'. Levin 2019 publishes no R_eff formula; the reference is the model's own output <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/audits/2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit.measurements.yaml#L4-L10>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-r-eff-n-100-g-gj-1-0-g-half-0-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-10-hopfield-k-sat-clause-energy-at-the-planted-assignment>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-11-natural-induction-delta-e-eta-n-2-at-eta-0-05-n-16>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-12-grn-conditioning-j-us-cs-after-t-15-pairings>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-13-brenner-exploratory-noise-variance-expansion-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-14-variational-free-energy-df-dt-at-kappa-0-5-grad-f-2-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-15-mortal-computation-t-surv-e-reserve-p-diss-p-harvest>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-16-shannon-hartley-c-1-2-log2-1-snr-at-snr-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-17-causal-emergence-2-0-delta-cp-i-on-s-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-18-o-information-omega-xor-3-from-the-explicit-joint-distribution>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-19-bode-waterbed-net-log-sensitivity-integral>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-levin-mafe-open-fraction-g-ij-g-0-at-v-i-v-j-60-mv-v-th-35-v-0-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-20-multicellular-pd-breakeven-cluster-size-and-first-strictly-dominant-cluster-size-b-2-c-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-21-fisher-natural-gradient-du-dt-at-lambda-min-2-grad-u-2-9>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-22-odd-elasticity-cycle-work-k12-k21-area>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-23-ephaptic-coupling-d-delta-phi-2-dt-at-g-eph-2-delta-phi-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-24-ca2-integral-feedback-steady-state-error-ca-ss-ca-target>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-25-nca-memory-transfer-error-after-4-halvings-from-e-0-64>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-boltzmann-ratio-c-post-c-ant-exp-40-mv-25-85-mv>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-4-galvanotaxis-cathodal-enrichment-exp-pe-e-at-pe-e-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-5-chvykov-low-rattling-log-log-slope-of-p-ss-vs-r-exit>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-6-epiplexity-l-f-e-f-h-f>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-7-secretary-problem-optimal-cutoff-k-and-success-probability-p-opt-for-n-100>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-8-polycomputing-truth-table-agreement-of-xor-and-or-observers-on-s-a-b>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-9-kan-outer-summand-count-2n-1-at-n-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-laws-whose-python-evaluation-computes-something-beyond-one-plugged-in-expression>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-laws-with-a-resolvable-doi-url-in-the-v1-audit-references>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-lean-theorems-that-quantify-universally-over-a-non-trivial-structural-statement>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-1> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.08"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "not faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-r-eff-n-100-g-gj-1-0-g-half-0-1> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 1 (TAME light cone) - R_eff(N=100, G_gj=1.0, G_half=0.1) = 91.0 cell_diameters" ;
        dcterms:description "No independent reference: Levin (2019, 2022) publish no R_eff formula; the equation is a Delphi O2 formalisation and the v1 reference 91.0 was the same expression" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "1 + 99 * 1.0/(1.0 + 0.1) re-evaluated; matches script L52" ;
        schema:name "Law 1 (TAME light cone) - R_eff(N=100, G_gj=1.0, G_half=0.1)" ;
        schema:unitText "cell_diameters" ;
        schema:value "91.0" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-10-hopfield-k-sat-clause-energy-at-the-planted-assignment> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 10 (Hopfield k-SAT) - clause energy at the planted assignment = 0 energy_units" ;
        dcterms:description "Not a measurement: a literal. The Lean theorem does prove the single-clause iff for all Bool triples" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Script L106 assigns the literal 0; no clause, literal or assignment exists in the code to re-evaluate" ;
        schema:name "Law 10 (Hopfield k-SAT) - clause energy at the planted assignment" ;
        schema:unitText "energy_units" ;
        schema:value "0" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-11-natural-induction-delta-e-eta-n-2-at-eta-0-05-n-16> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 11 (natural induction) - Delta E = -eta N^2 at eta = 0.05, N = 16 = -12.8 energy_units" ;
        dcterms:description "No independent reference; no network is instantiated, so the identity Delta E = -eta N^2 (which assumes s_i s_j Delta J_ij summed over all N^2 ordered pairs) is asserted, not observed" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "-0.05 * 256" ;
        schema:name "Law 11 (natural induction) - Delta E = -eta N^2 at eta = 0.05, N = 16" ;
        schema:unitText "energy_units" ;
        schema:value "-12.8" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-12-grn-conditioning-j-us-cs-after-t-15-pairings> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 12 (GRN conditioning) - J_US,CS after T = 15 pairings = 0.8 coupling_weight" ;
        dcterms:description "No independent reference; Pigozzi et al. (2025) report conditioning in continuous GRN ODEs, not a linear weight ramp" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "0.05 + 15 * 0.05" ;
        schema:name "Law 12 (GRN conditioning) - J_US,CS after T = 15 pairings" ;
        schema:unitText "coupling_weight" ;
        schema:value "0.8" .

